as the war in ukraine continues to  intensify more than 4 million refugees  have escaped the country anderson woman  has made it her mission to help refugees  who are now stuck at the u.s mexico  border victoria saha caught up with her  as she was bringing supplies there today  she joins us tonight with her story  victoria  ukrainians have been forced to flee  their homes for the last month many  going to neighboring countries and some  trying to make their way here to the  united states but are held up at the  border one henderson woman realized she  needed to help them with crucial  supplies and took the trip down there  today  i was like let's go you know nina  nadinova woke up at the crack of dawn  saturday morning to start her drive to  tijuana i feel like it's a humanitarian  crisis and  no matter what nationality you're from  what country you're from  you have to be a part of this for days  naida nova was collecting supplies such  as clothing dry food and hygiene  products for the ukrainian refugees at  the u.s mexico border they're forced to  you know sit like this for two days in a  chair  you know they have nowhere to sleep and  the kids are bored out of their minds  nadinova is russian she tells us she  felt an urge to stand by the people who  are being hurt by the leader of her  native country it's like kind of like  you have a bad relative who did  something bad and i feel responsible and  i want to make it up to  you know to people who my relatives hurt  she shares with us the devastating  images of the long lines of people  waiting to be seen by immigration and  most who have no choice but to camp  outside the majority of people who are  here they want to go back home you know  the question is will they be able to go  anytime soon i don't think so the  hundreds of ukrainian refugees were able  to escape to mexico because there were  no visa requirements for them but now  they're left waiting to be able to  reunite with loved ones on the other  side of the border  she says she will continue to make more  trips to the border and has also signed  up to take in refugees here in las vegas  if they needed a home
 

